__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Large generated data/output — regenerate via the pipeline (see README.md
# "Reproducibility" / CLAUDE.md "Data Test Range & Reproducibility") rather
# than tracking multi-GB binary parquet in git history. latest_run_*.log
# summaries at repo root are small, curated, and intentionally still tracked
# (the pattern below matches the raw stdout/stderr dumps, NOT that file).
output/

# graphify-out/: the interactive chart + report ARE tracked (graph.html,
# graph_standalone.html, graph.json, GRAPH_REPORT.md, manifest.json) so the
# knowledge graph is browsable on GitHub without regenerating it locally.
# Only the regenerable AST/semantic cache and machine-local scratch state
# (e.g. .graphify_python, a literal local filesystem path) are ignored.
graphify-out/cache/
graphify-out/.graphify_*

# logs/archive/: ad-hoc raw run logs (underscore-prefixed, e.g.
# _data_ibkr_run.log) that predate the fixes below and got tracked by the
# same bug class — same rationale, untracked here.
logs/archive/*.log

# Root-level *.log handling — rewritten 2026-07-20 as a robust allow-list
# after the same bug class recurred 3 times (2026-07-11, 2026-07-15,
# 2026-07-20): every prior fix here was a one-off pattern for that
# session's specific ad-hoc scratch-log naming convention (`*_stdout.log`,
# `*_out.log`, `*_out[0-9].log`, ...), and every session invents a
# slightly different convention (e.g. 2026-07-20's `near_miss_1M_fixed.log`,
# `analysis_bugd65_rerun.log` — no _out/_err suffix at all) that slips
# through. Now: ignore ALL *.log at repo root by default, explicitly
# un-ignore the curated latest_run_*.log summaries and the small number of
# pre-existing tracked exceptions, then re-ignore the specific stdout/
# stderr-dump sub-pattern that would otherwise be caught by the
# latest_run_*.log allow-list. Order matters in gitignore — last matching
# rule wins, so the re-ignore below MUST come after the allow-list above
# it. New scratch logs of ANY future naming convention are ignored by
# default now instead of requiring a new pattern each time. Does not touch
# output/ (already ignored above) or logs/archive/ (already ignored above).
/*.log
!/latest_run_*.log
!/analysis_overnight.log
!/analysis_overnight_err.log
!/latest_run_data_err.log
!/near_miss_remaining.log
latest_*_stdout.log
latest_*_stderr.log